  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "The smallest sum one could get by adding three different numbers from the set \\(\\{7, 25, -1, 12, -3\\}\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-3\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "\\(21\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "To make the sum as small as possible, choose the three smallest different numbers. Any other selection replaces at least one of these with a larger number and therefore increases the sum.\n\nOrdering the set gives\n\\[\n-3<-1<7<12<25.\n\\]\nThus the smallest sum is\n\\[\n(-3)+(-1)+7=-4+7=\\boxed{3},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
